    "text": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with comprehensive tests. Here's what was created:\n\n## BoundedStack Class\n- **Instance variables**: `elements` (array), `capacity` (max size), `count` (current size)\n- **Methods**:\n  - `capacity:` (class method) - Creates a stack with validation\n  - `initializeWithCapacity:` - Initializes the stack\n  - `push:` - Adds an object; fails with \"stack is full\" if at capacity\n  - `pop` - Removes and returns top element; fails with \"stack is empty\" if empty\n  - `top` - Returns top element without removing; fails with \"stack is empty\" if empty\n  - `isEmpty` - Returns true if stack is empty\n  - `size` - Returns current number of elements\n\n## Error Handling\n- Invalid capacity (0, negative, non-integer): \"capacity must be a positive integer\"\n- Push on full stack: \"stack is full\"\n- Pop/top on empty stack: \"stack is empty\"\n\n## Test Suite (13 tests, all passing)\n- Creating stacks with valid capacity\n- Rejecting invalid capacities (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Basic push/pop operations\n- Multiple push/pop sequences\n- Size tracking\n- Full stack behavior\n- Empty stack behavior\n- Top operation without modification\n- Different object types\n\nThe image has been saved with all code and tests in the `BoundedStack` and `BoundedStack-Tests` system categories."
